alfe: PROTOCOL-MOCK-CAD-FULL-LIFECYCLE flakes on a too-tight 2s wait timeout

== Symptom ==

`test:alfe:sbcl` (autolisp-front-end/tests, FiveAM) intermittently fails the
single test PROTOCOL-MOCK-CAD-FULL-LIFECYCLE — 5 of its checks, out of 584 total
in the suite (99% pass). Observed on the release-1.8.100 tag pipeline
(gitlab.com/ogamita/clautolisp pipeline 2780812581, runner on poseidon); the
adjacent release-1.8.99 pipeline (same relevant code) passed it.

Failure details (FiveAM):

    PROTOCOL-MOCK-CAD-FULL-LIFECYCLE ... .ffff.f.
    (ALFE.PROTOCOL.FILE:WAIT-FOR-STATUS-PREFIX SESSION "RUNNING" :TIMEOUT 2)
      was NIL.
    (ALFE.PROTOCOL.FILE:WAIT-FOR-STATUS-PREFIX SESSION "DONE" :TIMEOUT 2)
      was NIL.
    ... (the later transition assertions cascade off the first miss)

The test drives a mock CAD state machine in a background thread and waits for
each transition with the documented poll primitives, each with `:timeout 2`.
When the first "RUNNING" transition is not observed within 2 s, every
downstream assertion fails too.

== Context / likely cause ==

Timing flake, not a logic regression: the 2-second timeout is too tight when the
poseidon runner is loaded (many concurrent CI jobs share the box), so the
background thread + filesystem-status handshake occasionally does not reach
"RUNNING" within 2 s. It passed on the immediately-preceding tag with identical
protocol code; the only changes on 1.8.100 were the Windows C-build
(build-libredwg.sh) and the version bump, neither of which touches this path.

This matters because it gates releases: a flake here fails `test:alfe:sbcl`,
which skips the whole release stage (release:*, collect:release, publish:release
all skipped). For now the workaround is to retry the job.

== Suggested fix ==

Make the lifecycle test robust to a loaded runner, e.g.:
 - raise the poll timeout (2 s -> ~10 s), or make it configurable via an env var
   the CI sets higher, and/or
 - back the wait with a deadline-relative poll that tolerates scheduler jitter,
   and/or
 - mark the test `interruptible`/retryable, or split the timing-sensitive
   transitions from the pure-logic assertions.

== Repro ==

    make -C autolisp-front-end test-sbcl
    # under artificial load (e.g. `stress-ng --cpu N` or many parallel CI jobs)
    # PROTOCOL-MOCK-CAD-FULL-LIFECYCLE fails ~intermittently on WAIT-FOR-STATUS.

Found during the release-pipeline shakedown (documentation/release-pipeline.md);
does not block the pipeline design — retrying the job clears it.
